### F5 — `remap_single_linkage_tree` docstring mis-describes `non_finite` (name and type)
severity: medium
evidence: sklearn/cluster/_hdbscan/hdbscan.py:365-366 documents `non_finite : ndarray / Boolean array of which entries in the raw data are non-finite`. The single call site at sklearn/cluster/_hdbscan/hdbscan.py:838 passes `non_finite=set(infinite_index + missing_index)` — a Python `set` of integer indices. The function then uses `len(non_finite)` (line 369) as an offset for internal indices and enumerates it (line 388) to write raw indices into `outlier_tree`.
scenario: "reader trusts the docstring and passes a boolean mask (as documented) → offsets and outlier indices are wrong (e.g. `outlier_count = len(mask) = n_samples`, not `count of outliers`), producing silently corrupted tree remapping"
contract: Rewrite the parameter doc to describe `non_finite` as an iterable/set of integer indices (of the non-finite rows in the raw data).
